    "text": {
     "en": "A pictograph uses pictures or symbols to show data. A key tells how many each symbol stands for, for example one book picture is 5 books.\nA bar graph uses bars whose length shows the amount. Draw two axes, choose a scale such as 1 box for 5 books, and draw equal-width bars.\nAlways give the graph a title and label the axes."
    }
